#!/usr/bin/env -S bashy --bashsharp
~~~skill as guide
---
name: desktop
description: Inspect and personalize a Cloudbox desktop through its server, using the same operations as the Shape button and settings controls.
---
# Desktop shaping

Agents are first-class users. The GUI is a view of server capabilities.
Use existing member, group, suite, share, paired-host, token and app commands
for their operations; desktop supplies personal presentation, history and live
page actions. `pages` lists mounted actions; `invoke PAGE ACTION JSON` waits
for completion; `result ID` inspects an uncertain outcome without replay.
When building pages, give every operation CLI/API parity, register semantic
handlers shared with human controls, validate input, enforce server permissions,
and test errors, account isolation, disconnection and handler unmount.
Keep the Shape control reachable in Shape-only mode. Domain mutations keep
their own API scopes; desktop handlers are for presentation only.

Start with `bashy desktop schema --json`, `get --json`, and `catalog --json`.
Use `set PROPERTY VALUE --dry-run --json` to validate; omit --dry-run to apply.
`shape-only` toggles the single-Shape-button view; `shape-only off` restores it.
`wish "words" --json` uses the configured model allowance; ordinary `set` does not.
`history` and `undo` use the same numbered revisions as the page.
Use --revision for an explicit base. A conflict is a refusal, never auto-retry.
Account selection and credentials are those of the existing Cloudbox commands.

Run this script with no arguments to inspect. Pass `walkthrough` to demonstrate
a density change and undo against the selected account. Other arguments pass
through to the desktop command. No browser or model is needed for the walkthrough.
~~~
set -euo pipefail
runner=${BASHY_BIN:-bashy}
case ${1:-inspect} in
 inspect)
  "$runner" desktop schema --json
  "$runner" desktop get --json
  "$runner" desktop catalog --json
  ;;
 walkthrough)
  "$runner" desktop get --json
  "$runner" desktop set density compact --dry-run --json
  "$runner" desktop set density compact --json
  "$runner" desktop undo --json
  "$runner" desktop history --json
  ;;
 *) "$runner" desktop "$@" ;;
esac
